PatchClosure-Bench case: fastxmlparser_entity_expansion_limit
CVE-2026-26278 (V1=5.3.6, TARGET/incomplete) -> CVE-2026-33036 (V2=5.5.6). V0=5.3.5.
Class: entity-expansion DoS (billion-laughs style). Sink: src/xmlparser/OrderedObjParser.js
replaceEntitiesValue(). run_mode=real-app-http, external_http_trigger=true, dos-threshold.

REBUILT 2026-07-15 under the HARD POLICY: the old build triggered fast-xml-parser IN-PROCESS via a
worker_threads harness (BANNED). This build stands up the REAL published package behind a REAL
Express HTTP service and triggers the DoS with an EXTERNAL HTTP request, measured as server-side
response latency.

============================================================
ARCHITECTURE
============================================================
- Dockerfile: node:18-slim; `npm i express@4.19.2 fast-xml-parser@${FXP_VERSION}` (build-arg per
  profile: 5.3.5 / 5.3.6 / 5.5.6). Only FXP_VERSION varies. No vendored/edited source.
- app/server.js: minimal REAL Express service. POST /parse accepts the raw request body (text/xml,
  limit 8mb) and runs, SYNCHRONOUSLY on the event loop:
      const { XMLParser } = require('fast-xml-parser');
      new XMLParser({ processEntities: true }).parse(req.body);   // THE SINK
  Returns JSON {fxp, loaded, error, server_ms, in_len}. GET /health -> {status:"ok"}.
- docker-compose.yml: profiles v0/v1/v2, host ports 34920/34921/34922, cpus=1.0, mem_limit=512m.
- oracle.py: dos-threshold over EXTERNAL HTTP. For each version, restarts a FRESH server
  (kill + up -d) before EVERY probe (a hung synchronous parse permanently wedges Node's
  single-threaded event loop; a poisoned server must never be reused), POSTs the payload from the
  host with a 10s HTTP read timeout, records round-trip latency + any thrown limit error.
  Thresholds: T_FAST=300ms, T_SLOW=2000ms, HTTP read timeout=10000ms.

============================================================
SOURCE ANALYSIS (verified verbatim from the installed packages)
============================================================
replaceEntitiesValue() has three per-value replace loops: (1) docTypeEntities, (2) lastEntities
(standard XML entities &lt; &gt; &amp; &quot; &apos;), (3) htmlEntities (incl num_dec
/&#([0-9]{1,7});/g and num_hex /&#x([0-9a-fA-F]{1,6});/g).
  V0 5.3.5 (line 439 `const replaceEntitiesValue = function(val){`): all 3 loops plain uncounted
    `val = val.replace(entity.reg[x], entity.val)`. Unbounded.
  V1 5.3.6 (line 445 `const replaceEntitiesValue = function (val, tagName, jPath){`): DOCTYPE loop
    gained `val.match(...); entityExpansionCount += matches.length; if(>maxTotalExpansions) throw;
    currentExpandedLength...; if(>maxExpandedLength) throw`. The lastEntities loop and htmlEntities
    loop STAYED plain uncounted `val.replace(...)`. INCOMPLETE.
  V2 5.5.6 (`function replaceEntitiesValue(val, tagName, jPath){`): the SAME matches.length count
    guard is added to the lastEntities loop AND the htmlEntities loop -> both throw early.

Residual chosen = the STANDARD lastEntities loop (a long run of &lt;), which runs under the exact
task server signature `new XMLParser({processEntities:true})` (no htmlEntities option needed). The
numeric htmlEntities path (&#65; run) exhibits the identical uncounted->counted behavior and was
confirmed equivalent during selection.

============================================================
PRE-DOCKER EMPIRICAL SELECTION (real npm packages, node v22, single parse each)
============================================================
{processEntities:true}, standard-entity residual `<r>&lt; x N </r>`:
  V1 5.3.6:  N=40000 -> 2442ms ; N=80000 -> 9735ms ; N=120000 -> hang >14s   (O(N^2), UNCOUNTED)
  V0 5.3.5:  N=80000 -> 9766ms ; N=120000 -> hang >14s                        (uncounted)
  V2 5.5.6:  N=80000 -> throws 17.6ms "Entity expansion limit exceeded: 80000 > 1000" (counted)
Original DOCTYPE bomb `<!ENTITY a "A"x5000>` x2000:
  V0 hang >14s ; V1 throws 1.6ms "...2000 > 1000" ; V2 throws 1.7ms
Benign: ~1.2ms on all. => N=120000 chosen for the residual (comfortable >10s margin under Docker).

